[ddtrace]
; The ddraw.dll the game's calls go on to, a path or a file name in the game's folder.
; Empty: Windows' own (System32's ddraw.dll).
; In front of dd2d9: rename dd2d9's ddraw.dll to dd2d9.dll and set target=dd2d9.dll
; In front of another wrapper: rename its ddraw.dll (real.dll, say) and set target=real.dll
target=
